            'The name \'Bharatavarsha\' (country of the Bharatas) from the Mahabharata, and \'Jambudvipa\' (island of the jamun tree) were used to describe the entire Indian Subcontinent. \'Bharat\' became the widely accepted name, mentioned in texts like the Vishnu Purana, which described India as the land between the Himalayas and the ocean.',
