            'A democracy is a system where the power rests with the people, either directly or through elected representatives. This is important because it ensures that everyone has a say in how they are governed. In a democracy, the government is divided into three organs: the Legislature (makes laws), the Executive (implements laws), and the Judiciary (interprets laws). These organs work together with a system of checks and balances to prevent any one organ from becoming too powerful.',
